# ts_advertise.cfg holds the Discord bot token. Never commit it.
#
# The token is the whole bot account, not access to one channel.
# If it ever lands in a commit, Reset Token in the Discord developer portal:
# removing the file afterwards does not help, the history keeps it.
ts/addons/amxmodx/configs/ts_advertise.cfg

# Runtime state written by the bot, not source.
discord-bot/rsvp.json
discord-bot/bot.log
discord-bot/bot.err
discord-bot/__pycache__/
rcbot/bot_playerids.ini

# H9 Stuff
*.backup
# Binary backups beside a rebuilt DLL or EXE (<file>.bak_<tag>) stay in TSM: git is the backup.
*.bak_*
# The map pipeline's outputs, when its scripts run in a checkout: the maps that ship are under
# ts/maps, and export-map/ holds the sources and generators.
export-map/**/out/
export-map/**/tmp/
# Metamod-R's build output. Upstream's own .gitignore is left out of the mirror (export.bat):
# it ignores *.bat, and with it msvc/PreBuild.bat, which the Windows build runs.
metamod-r/**/msvc/Release*/
metamod-r/**/msvc/Debug*/
metamod-r/**/msvc/.vs/
metamod-r/**/msvc/*.user
metamod-r/metamod/version/appversion.h

# Files Xash writes into the game folder while it runs, for anyone playing from here.
H9XASH/**/video.cfg
H9XASH/**/opengl.cfg
H9XASH/**/.xash_id
H9XASH/**/.fontcache/
H9XASH/**/voice_ban.dt
H9XASH/**/custom.hpk
# The settings Xash keeps in valve, and the app id the Steam broker writes.
H9XASH/valve/config.cfg
H9XASH/**/steam_appid.txt
H9XASH/**/save/
H9XASH/**/logs/
H9XASH/**/screenshots/
H9XASH/ts_downloads/
H9XASH/*.log
H9XASH/ts/menu_music_resolved.cfg

# What building xash3d-fwgs here leaves behind. FWGS's own .gitignore files are left out of the
# mirror (export.bat): written for its submodule layout, they ignore Makefile, CMakeLists.txt and
# source folders the submodules track, which the engine build needs. FWGS's CI signing
# certificate (scripts/fwgs.pfx, a key container) is left out too.
xash3d-fwgs/**/*.pfx
xash3d-fwgs/build/
xash3d-fwgs/waf3-*/
xash3d-fwgs/.lock-waf*
# and the SDL2 download and install staging xash.bat keeps beside itself.
xash3d-h9-patches/deps/
xash3d-h9-patches/stage/

# H9XASH's server side. The Discord bot token never goes in (the same rule as ts/
# above), nor the server's logs and runtime state.
H9XASH/ts/addons/amxmodx/configs/ts_advertise.cfg
H9XASH/ts/addons/amxmodx/logs/
H9XASH/ts/addons/amxmodx/data/vault/
H9XASH/ts/addons/amxmodx/data/vault.ini
H9XASH/ts/addons/amxmodx/data/tsstats.dat
H9XASH/rcbot/bot_playerids.ini
# A player's own settings: config.cfg holds their player id (cl_h9_userid). New players start
# from the tracked ts/config.stock.cfg, which h9xash.bat copies to ts/config.cfg when there is none.
H9XASH/ts/config.cfg
H9XASH/ts/config.cfg.bak
H9XASH/ts/console_history.txt

# H9XASH: generated server-list files, and the Steam binaries (their licence is not settled).
H9XASH/ts/xashcomm.lst
H9XASH/ts/networking_resolved.cfg

# H9XASH: redundant resolved configs
H9XASH/ts/menu_music_resolved.cfg
H9XASH/ts/menu_bg_video_resolved.cfg

# The list bot: its token and heartbeat key, and its logs. Only the template is tracked.
serverlist-bot/serverlist.cfg
serverlist-bot/serverlist.log
serverlist-bot/__pycache__/
generate_patches.log
H9XASH/discord-bot/bot.log
H9XASH/discord-bot/bot.pid
H9XASH/user_id.ini
H9XASH/ts/demoheader.tmp
H9XASH/ts/userid_resolved.cfg
H9XASH/discord-bot/bot.log

# wad2png output: the PNGs are generated, only the folder is kept.
wad2png/exported/*
!wad2png/exported/.keep

# The Discord bot token's files and any copy of them, anywhere in the tree: ts_advertise.cfg,
# and ts_advertise_local.cfg, the one ts_advertise_local.cfg.example says to make. The list
# bot's token and heartbeat key likewise. Only the .example templates are tracked.
ts_advertise*.cfg*
!ts_advertise*.cfg.example

# The presence plugin's key for h9web (h9_presence.sma, docs/H9_PRESENCE.txt), and any copy of it,
# anywhere in the tree: whoever has it can report players onto that server. A hand-made key sits
# in h9_presence.cfg (only the .example template is tracked), an enrolled one in h9_presence.key.
# And the per-install device id the id proof uses, which is never shared.
h9_presence.cfg*
!h9_presence.cfg.example
h9_presence.key*
device_id.ini*
serverlist-bot/serverlist.cfg*
!serverlist-bot/serverlist.cfg.example

# A player's own files, wherever a game folder sits: the H9 id (H9XASH writes it from
# user_id.ini at every launch), Xash's id, and the console history, which keeps whatever was
# typed, an rcon_password included.
user_id.ini*
userid_resolved.cfg
.xash_id
console_history.txt
history_servers.lst

# Records of other people, wherever a game or bot folder sits: AMX Mod X's logs (names, Steam
# ids, addresses, admin logins), its TS stats, the server's ban lists, the bot's RSVPs.
**/addons/amxmodx/logs/
tsstats.dat
banned.cfg
listip.cfg
rsvp.json

# Windows' thumbnail caches: they keep pictures of what was in a folder, deleted files too.
Thumbs.db

# The web client's build, copied in at deploy time (havoc9.org/webclient/DEPLOY.txt): generated,
# and the game package alone is over a gigabyte.
havoc9.org/webclient/engine/
havoc9.org/webclient/game/
havoc9.org/webclient/manifest.json
havoc9.org/webclient/preload.json
webclient-build/

# Python writes these beside any script it runs: never source.
__pycache__/

# Client ZIPs and their reports from stage-h9xash.cmd, and older hand-made ZIPs of H9XASH. Of dist\,
# only the updater (tools\updater\build.cmd makes it) and the .keep file that holds the folder are tracked.
/dist/*
!/dist/H9XASH-Updater.exe
!/dist/.keep
# The updater's build folder: its venv, PyInstaller's work files and caches.
tools/updater/.build/
/H9XASH.zip
/H9XASH-*.zip

# h9web's keys and backups, anywhere in the tree (h9web/README.txt sections 7 and 10). None of
# them is ever safe to ship or commit: secrets.json (the password pepper and the player id key:
# with it and a copy of the database, every password can be attacked offline), data.key (it
# opens the Discord links in the database), any other *.key, h9web-backup's archives (*.h9backup:
# the database, and with --with-keys the keys too) and their unfinished .partial files, the
# backup passphrase file, h9web's data folders, and .env files. The CA bundles (cacert.pem) and
# mbedTLS's test keys under xash3d-fwgs/3rdparty are public, so those stay tracked.
secrets.json
data.key
*.key
!xash3d-fwgs/3rdparty/**/*.key
*.h9backup
*.h9backup.partial
backup-passphrase*
h9web/data/
h9web-local/
.env
/H9XASH/ts/downloads
H9XASH/ts/addons/amxmodx/data/tsm_music.txt

# Never source: a CMake build tree (the SDHLT tools' build-win64 held object files and local paths), a process's pid file,
# any log, and the .bak copy Xash or a tool leaves beside a config. Files tracked before this rule stay tracked until
# they are removed with `git rm --cached`.
export-map/**/build-win64/
*.pid
*.log
*.bak

# Code-signing certificates and their keys: whoever has one can sign as this project.
*.pfx
*.p12

# Operator notes kept on the maintainer's PC only (hosting layout, runbooks, local paths): never published.
ops-private/

# The static site assembled by tools/build-site.mjs (generated, never committed)
/site/
